          "type": "input",
          "title": "You'll want to know: ಕಟ್ಟುನಿಟ್ಟು",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "ಕಟ್ಟುನಿಟ್ಟು — kaṭṭuniṭṭu — \"strictness\"."
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "ಪರೀಕ್ಷೆಯ ಸಮಯದಲ್ಲಿ ನಿಯಮಗಳು ಕಟ್ಟುನಿಟ್ಟಾಗಿ ಇರುತ್ತವೆ. parīkṣeya samayadalli niyamagaḷu kaṭṭuniṭṭāgi iruttave. During exams the rules are strict."
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "ಕಟ್ಟುನಿಟ್ಟಾದ, strict; ಕಟ್ಟುನಿಟ್ಟಾಗಿ, strictly."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "index": 2,
          "type": "etymology",
          "title": "The word, taken apart",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "ಕಟ್ಟುನಿಟ್ಟು (kaṭṭuniṭṭu) is native Kannada, a pair-word built on kaṭṭu, \"to bind, a restraint\" (DEDR 1147); the second half, niṭṭu, is not settled."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "index": 3,
          "type": "notice",
          "title": "What you've built",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "One more word for saying what happens if."
            }
